0 Basidiocarps small, marasmioid; stipe insititious, filiform or not, glabrous, pruinose, finely pubescent or hairy011313702
0 Basidiocarps larger, collybioid, rarely tricholomatoid; stipe never insititious, never filiform, glabrous, pubescent or fibrillose; cheilocystidia never in the form of broom cells; pileipellis never hymeniform also in primordial stage, without broom cells011413806
0  (1)  Stipe filiform, glabrous, pruinose or finely pubescent; cheilocystidia in the form of broom cells or coralloid elements; pileipellis hymeniform in primordial stages, soon an irregular trichoderm, often mixed with single broom cells023514903
0 Stipe filiform or not, pubescent to hairy, dark coloured, especielly in lower part; context often with unpleasant smell; rhizomorphs absent; pileipellis an ixocutis consisting of cylindrical hyphae without Ramealis-structure; cheilocystidia absent or scattered and indistinct0236141004
0  (2) Stipe blackish brown, glabrous, shilling; pileus chocolate-brown or dark pinkish brown with pinkish yellow to pale pink margin; lamellae incarnate to pinkish brown; on sticks, needles and leaves of coniferous and deciduous trees and shrubs (if smell of rotten cabbage and stipe hairy, cf. Gymnopus perforons) 035715110G. androsaceus0
0 Stipe sordid red-brown, finely hairy, especially when young, glabrescens with âge; pileus pale pink or pinkish brown with pale, almost white margin; lamellae white to pale cream coloured; on dead leaves of Quercus 035815120G. quercophilus0
0  (2) Basidiocarps small, collybioid; pileus 6-8 mm broad, when moist dark yellowish brown; stipe 5 x 1.3-1.5 mm, yellow-brown, very minutely granular or pruinose in same colour; context with indistinct smell; spores 7.0-8.5 x 4.0-5.0 pin; clamps absent; on bark of a deciduous tree 046916130 G. bisporiger0
0 Basidiocarps larger, marasmioid or collybioid; stipe 15-40 mm long; context with unpleasant smell; clamps present04610161405
0  (4) Basidiocarp omphalioid or collybioid; pileus 8-30 mm broad, red-brown, yellow-brown or brown ochraceous, pallescent to ochraceous red on drying; stipe 15-30 (40) x \-4 mm, cylindrical to tapering towards base, sometimes laterally compressed, entirely pruinose- hairy with dark hairs; caulocystidia scattered, especially in upper part of stipe; on dead branches, sticks, etc. of deciduous trees and scrubs 05101117150G. foetidus0
0 Basidiocarps marasmioid; pileus 5-15 (20) mm broad, when moist pinkish brown, pallescent on drying; stipe 15-40 x 0.5-1 mm, filiform, at apex concolorous with pileus, in lower parts dark brown to black, hairy; context with unpleasant, fetid smell like rotten cabbage; caulocystidia abundant; on fallen needles of Picea, rarely also Pinus and Abies 05101217160 G. perforans0
0  (1)  Stipe 50-110 (160) x 8-20 mm, red-brown, fusoid or irregularly compressed, strongly fibrillose-costate, tapering towards a deeply rooting base 0641318170 G. fusipes0
0 Stipe différent06414181807
0  (6)  Smell strong, unpleasant, reminisccnt of rotten cabbage, sewage, onions or garlic .071415191908
0 Smell indistinct0714161920017
0  (7)  Pileus pinkish brown, ochraceous-pink, pale (pinkish) brown, pale red-brown, strongly pallescent on drying; lamellae often rather crowded081517202109
0 Pileus and/or stipe darker; lamellae moderately distant to very distant0815182022010
