0  (14)  Pileus dark red-brown when moist, pallescent to pinkish or ochraceous grey-brown on drying; lamellae more crowded (26-34), darker, almost concolorous with pileus; stipe entirely pruinose, then almost smooth and glabrous to slightly fibrillose, uniformly dark brown; spores (7.5) 8.0-11 (12) x (3.0) 3.3-4.5 pm 015293127350 G. dysosmus0
0 Pileus dark brown with pink or reddish tinge, darker at centre, paler at margin, pallescent on drying to sordid ochraceous brown, pinkish brown or greyish brown; lamellae pale cream then pale pinkish or greyish-brownish; stipe lilac, pinkish or sordid brown with paler, pinkish yellow apex, glabrescent with âge; spores (5.5) 6.5-9.0 (9.5) x (2.9) 3.2- 4.5 pm 015293227360G. impudicus0
