0  (45) Pileus campanulate to convex, then plano-convex with depressed centre, finally in- fundibuliform, weak red to dusky red with pale red margin; stipe apparently glabrous, but completely pruinose under lens; context with slightly farinaceous smell and taste; spores 5.5- 7.5 (8.0) pm wide, broadly ellipsoid, rarely subglobose; basidia (30) 35-47 x (8.5) 9.5- 13 pm; well-developed cheilocystidia absent; pileipellis with numerous cylindrical, subfusoid to subclavate terminal cells; 011 soil, mossy banks, among fallen, decaying leaves of Quercus ilex ssp. bal Iota and Pinus pinea 046929358970G. castaneus0
